📗
  🛡 A set of response headers that tell a browser to be careful with what it
  is given, and the layer that puts them on every answer:

    🧱 app 🛡 app 🆕🛡❗️❗️❗️

  A new one has X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, so that a file is not run
  as something its type does not say it is; X-Frame-Options: DENY, so that
  no other site can show the app inside a frame and have its buttons
  clicked there; and Referrer-Policy: same-origin, so that the addresses of
  the app's pages are not handed to the sites they link to, while the app's
  own pages go on saying where they are. (With no-referrer a browser sends
  Origin: null with every form it posts, the app's own included, which a
  check of origins then cannot tell from a stranger's.) An answer that has
  one of them already keeps its own. Every setter returns the shield.
