  📗
    Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=seconds; includeSubDomains, which
    tells a browser to come to this host and its subdomains over HTTPS only,
    for that long. Zero or less takes the header out. It is not there unless
    this is called: the server cannot see whether the proxy in front of it
    speaks HTTPS, and a browser that has been told this over HTTP by mistake
    remembers it.
